disclose.io diodb (https://github.com/disclose/diodb)
  Program directory data, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0
  Universal: https://github.com/disclose/diodb/blob/master/LICENSE

CISA dotgov-data (https://github.com/cisagov/dotgov-data)
  The list of US federal .gov domains used as the security.txt seed list,
  dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.

security.txt files (RFC 9116)
  Each program record from the securitytxt adapter is derived from the
  security.txt file its domain publishes for automated retrieval; the
  record's provenance names the file. The policies those files link to
  belong to their publishers and are not copied into the bundles.

arkadiyt/bounty-targets-data (https://github.com/arkadiyt/bounty-targets-data)
projectdiscovery/public-bugbounty-programs (https://github.com/projectdiscovery/public-bugbounty-programs)
  Public aggregate datasets of bug-bounty program listings, both MIT licensed
  as repositories. The listings come from the platforms they name and remain
  subject to those platforms' terms: records of a platform are published in
  the signed feed only when the publish policy (policy/platforms.json) allows
  it, with the attribution text recorded there. Removal requests: TAKEDOWN.md.

Program names, policies and terms remain the property of the organisations
that publish them. Listing a program in the feed does not imply that the
organisation endorses OpenCTEM, nor that any testing is authorised.
